@prefix esaog:  <https://w3id.org/esaog/core#> .
@prefix owl:    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix prov:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix skos:   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix agento: <http://www.w3id.org/agentic-ai/onto#> .

# Alignment module (kept out of the reasoning closure used in experiments).
#
# REUSE STATUS (verified September 2026):
#  * PROV-O is reused directly inside esaog-core.ttl (no redundant terms):
#    esaog:Actor rdfs:subClassOf prov:Agent, esaog:Execution rdfs:subClassOf
#    prov:Activity, esaog:Artifact rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity.
#  * AgentO (Ekelhart et al., ESWC 2026): namespace and class names verified
#    against the released ontology file
#    https://github.com/agentic-patterns/agentic-ai-onto/blob/main/ontology.ttl
#    (MIT licence), whose declared ontology IRI is
#    <http://www.w3id.org/agentic-ai/onto>; the documentation redirect is
#    https://w3id.org/agentic-ai/onto. Only SKOS mapping links are asserted
#    (no owl:equivalentClass), so the alignment cannot change any entailment
#    used by the orchestrator. AgentO has no class for a concrete workflow
#    instance; esaog:Workflow is therefore only related to agento:WorkflowPattern.
#  * PROV-AGENT (Souza et al., IEEE eScience 2025): the model is published as a
#    conceptual extension of W3C PROV (implemented in ORNL Flowcept,
#    https://github.com/ORNL/flowcept) without an RDF namespace, so no RDF links
#    can be asserted. The correspondence is documented here instead; because both
#    PROV-AGENT and ESAOG specialise PROV-O, ESAOG provenance records remain
#    interpretable at the PROV-O level:
#        esaog:Agent       ~ PROV-AGENT AIAgent           (both prov:Agent)
#        esaog:Invocation  ~ PROV-AGENT AgentTool          (both prov:Activity)
#        (no ESAOG term)   ~ PROV-AGENT AIModelInvocation  (LLM calls are logged
#                                                           as run metadata, not in G_E)
#        esaog:Artifact    ~ PROV-AGENT ResponseData / DomainData (both prov:Entity)
#  * ESAOG-specific terms (Capability-as-class punning, clearance levels,
#    mustBeRealizedBy obligations, runtime Failure subclasses) have no
#    counterpart in either vocabulary; they are minted in the esaog: namespace.

esaog:Agent         skos:closeMatch   agento:Agent .
esaog:Tool          skos:closeMatch   agento:Tool .
esaog:Task          skos:closeMatch   agento:Task .
esaog:Goal          skos:closeMatch   agento:Goal .
esaog:Capability    skos:closeMatch   agento:Capability .
esaog:Step          skos:closeMatch   agento:WorkflowStep .
esaog:Workflow      skos:relatedMatch agento:WorkflowPattern .
